.TH "FLOX\-UPGRADE" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-upgrade \- upgrade packages in an environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general\-options>] upgrade
     [\-d=<path> | \-r=<owner>/<name>]
     [\-\-dry\-run]
     [<package or pkg\-group>]...
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Upgrade packages in the environment.
.PP
When no arguments are specified, all packages in the environment are
upgraded if possible.
A package is upgraded if its version, build configuration, or dependency
graph changes.
.PP
Packages to upgrade can be specified by group name.
Packages without a specified pkg\-group in the manifest are placed in a
group named `toplevel'.
The packages in that group can be upgraded without updating any other
groups by passing `toplevel' as the group name.
.PP
A single package can only be specified to upgrade by ID if it is not in
a group with any other packages.
.PP
See \f[B]\f[CB]manifest.toml(5)\f[B]\f[R] for more on using pkg\-groups.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Upgrade Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]
Show available upgrades but do not apply them.
.TP
\f[CR]<package or pkg\-group>\f[R]
Install ID or pkg\-group to upgrade.
.SS Environment Options
If no environment is specified for an environment command, the
environment in the current directory or the active environment that was
last activated is used.
.TP
\f[CR]\-d\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R]
Path containing a .flox/ directory.
.TP
\f[CR]\-r\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-reference\f[R]
A FloxHub environment, specified in the form \f[CR]<owner>/<name>\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]\-D\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-default\f[R]
Use your default environment (\f[CR]<your\-user>/default\f[R]).
When unauthenticated in an interactive context, you will be prompted to
log in.
In non\-interactive contexts (e.g., scripts or CI), this flag will fail
with an error when authentication is missing.
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
